WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.370
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.370
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.220
Special Vehicles Department 2

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.980
The blue soaring sky...

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.360
the still surface of water,
sardine-colored clouds.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.950
In a brief, fleeting shadow,
autumn comes to the capitol.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.040
Too many syllables...
oh, well.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.330
It's almost time.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.710
At 1200 hours, Division 2
takes over the active shift.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.300
It's all yours, now.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.220
I verify the hand-over.
Division 2 is now on call.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:41.800
Leaving so soon?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.100
They're overhauling
all my Labors tomorrow...

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.390
and we spent all night
chasing after a false alarm.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.020
I'm taking the day off.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.980
Have fun!

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.320
She's so cute!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.950
...understand? This new
machine is just a blank slate.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.580
It only has software
for basic motions.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:17.130
But its movements will smooth
out as it learns your patterns.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.630
So he's like a baby,
waiting to be taught?

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.100
More like a
newly-built computer.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.020
It's only brought to life by the
movements it learns from you.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.600
So don't ever forget
to back up your data.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.150
Did you bring
your training data?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.530
Forty hours worth!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.240
Make it a habit to back up
after each session.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.700
That data is your
most valuable asset.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.660
Install it now,
before you forget.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.790
"A Labor is a mirror that
reflects the heart of its pilot."

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.710
It's all up to you, whether you
become an ace or a liability.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.040
That may be tough.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.460
You may feel sentimental
about your regular machine...

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.970
but the only unique aspect
is the data stored in ROM.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:10.730
If you copy the data to machine 3,
that's now your machine.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.770
Clearly, you don't
really understand that...

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.360
since you've so gleefully
marked up your machine.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.240
But Ota's under your command...

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.360
and he customized the
head on machine 2.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.200
That was Ota's doing.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.080
Division 2: Prepare for Ready
Status. Load the carriers.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.580
I repeat, load the carriers.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.350
Machine 2. Board.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.940
Why doesn't he use
auto guidance?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:00.610
The 98's carrier has auto
guidance for carrier boarding.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.070
Ota, I'll give you one try.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.530
Piece of cake.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.700
Not so rough!

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.130
And now, machine 1.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.470
Manually?
You're kidding!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.390
What's with the peanut gallery?

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:38.560
This is kind of an initiation ritual.
Didn't I tell you?

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.190
No, you didn't.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.070
You'll be fine.
Just relax.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.570
Come on, machine 1.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.330
She'll do it.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.630
Miss Izumi, you'll lose your
balance if you're too cautious.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.380
Don't think about it;
just move into it.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.500
Roger.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.900
Machine 1: Loaded!

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.110
Good work, Noa!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.620
Just barely.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.540
That was a close one.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.790
Don't be a sore loser.
Next customer!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.290
She's not half bad.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.540
Let's see how she gets
along in Second Section.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:47.630
She's young;
she'll adapt. Also...

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.680
she has an affinity
for her machine.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.220
I respect that.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.890
That may be more
of a problem.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:04.730
...so sometimes we take over
for the police or riot squad...

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:08.070
but usually we just
wait here on standby.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.530
But, Officer Yamazaki...

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.030
Call me Hiromi.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:15.490
Hiromi, what do we do
while we're waiting?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.290
We wait for the call,
whenever it might come.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.540
It's rough duty, staying ready
24 hours a day, 7 days a week.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:27.670
That's why we have
plenty of other activities.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.390
All duty members and all
mechanics: Prepare for a 606.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.550
Bring your 03 units
to the hanger.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.600
I repeat...
Oh, forget it.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.560
A 606? 03 units?

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:41.640
This.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.450
Not again!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.070
You have rotten luck.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.830
I'll end this losing streak!

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.920
Try it again!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:07.800
Lucky guy.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:13.300
It's your turn tomorrow. We use
the reserve machine... number 3.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.640
It's vital to train and
collect movement data.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:24.440
One more time! You're too slow
between the draw and lock-on.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.600
I know!

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.650
Then do it right!

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.070
Your target is the
captain's office!

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.280
The captain's office!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.740
The DC-11 overhead!

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:37.280
Eleven!

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.550
The basement
of the Shanghai!

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.840
Basement?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.020
Huh?

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.530
Is this okay?

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:55.650
What?

00:09:55.780 --> 00:10:00.410
Is it okay to waste time
fishing while we're on call?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:05.370
Do you think we're just goofing
off? What did you eat for lunch?

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.250
I had take-out fried rice.
It was delicious.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.670
And what'll you do tonight,
or tomorrow morning?

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:16.630
Only the Shanghai Restaurant
delivers way out here...

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.050
and only for lunch. At night
we're abandoned like stray dogs.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.140
We hit the grocery
when we can.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:26.310
The closest convenience store
is a 45-minute round-trip.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.520
But there isn't enough
food for all the men here...

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.980
and food is the most important
aspect to good morale.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.450
So we're forced to
be self-sufficient.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.910
Staples like rice and
noodles are easy to store.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.540
But what do we do about
protein, vitamins, and minerals?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:52.330
Hiromi grows tomatoes, which
handles the vitamins in season.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.420
But what about protein?

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.840
Don't you have
a henhouse?

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:01.590
Do you think we can get by on
the eggs from just 20 hens?

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.100
But Tokyo Bay is right here.
It's an aquatic treasure trove.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.980
Why not use it?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.980
You must be joking.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.360
Sometimes the daily struggle
overshadows police duty.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:21.860
Here in Special Vehicles, Second
Section, food is our passion!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.660
And if you can't find food...
you become a hungry ghoul!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.420
Good luck!
Come back soon!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.050
If you fail,
don't come back!

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.510
What's that?

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.930
The mechanics' pride:
Our police speedboat.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:47.100
You can do it!
We'll be waiting!

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:54.480
It's our secret weapon
for offshore fishing!

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:01.820
Model 97 Python

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.830
Tyrant

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.920
Goodbye, sir!

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.300
You must be tired,
Miss Izumi.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.020
We've been doing the
same stuff for six days.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.140
You'll get used to it.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.480
Our day-to-day struggles
are for food and territory.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:39.480
You make us
sound like dogs.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.570
Yes, a pack of stray dogs.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.610
That tea looks really foamy.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.780
It's carbonated.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.740
Report from the kitchen
team. 808 now in progress.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.240
Dinnertime!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.710
That wasn't tea!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:01.210
It's gone.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.850
We cook in shifts.
It's your turn tomorrow.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.890
Damn, the same
old goby fish.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.560
Hey, there are people
starving in China!

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.110
Emergency!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.860
The speedboat has run aground!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.620
Please, you have to
help us save the catch!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:34.330
Forget that, save the speedboat!
If it sinks, we're dead men!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.790
Asuma, please!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.710
You'll owe me.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.350
Go ahead! All clear!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.640
Are you sure this is okay?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.230
Labors were invented
for this type of work.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:00.940
But still...

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:04.150
Stay out of my way
and let me work!

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.780
What if...

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:09.490
What if what?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.290
What if he falls into the water?
What'll we do then?

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.500
Ota has over 250
hours piloting Labors.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.130
What are they
up to, out there?

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:45.530
With Ota out, it's up to
you and machine 1.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:47.900
I can't do that!

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.110
Alphonse will rust!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:55.830
I'm sure I could do
the job, in machine 3.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:06.130
Good thing Sakaki's gone.
if he saw this...

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:09.340
I'll dump you all in the sea!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.030
What? Are you sure?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:31.410
Who else would be coming
out here, this time of night?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.620
WHAT?

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.040
SHUT UP!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:53.890
What's wrong,
Mr. Sakaki?

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:57.930
I need to pick up the papers for
tomorrow's presentation at HQ.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:10.240
I'll... finish them up tonight
and drive them out to you!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:11.780
You will?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:16.030
Just leave it all to me!
We've been so busy lately...

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:19.700
you really deserve
to have a night off!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.540
All right, Shige.
If you say so.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.840
Now's our chance!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:37.430
What if a mobilization order
comes in while we're busy?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.560
Sometimes you have to
grab the bull by the horns.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.860
You'll wash him off
afterward, won't you?

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.570
I'll wash it, I'll wash it!
It'll be good as new!

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.460
I thought so.
They're up to something.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:13.840
He is?!

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.390
He must have been watching us!
What do we do?

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.640
We'll destroy the evidence,
and hope nobody talks.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.640
Let's get going!
Sakaki is on his way back!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.650
Hurry up,
I need the command car!

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.700
Whatever it takes,
we have to delay Sakaki.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:57.130
Okay, let's go. With drying off
time, we only have 20 minutes.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.840
But that's...

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.760
That's all the time that
Asuma can buy us.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.450
Damn!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.040
Breathe in here.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.920
But aren't you with
Special Vehicles?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:33.130
They needed the manpower.
Next!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.380
Shinohara here.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:42.470
Sakaki's left the line. He's
going around through Itobashi.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.640
Roger! Go set up the net...
I'll be right behind you.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:12.420
Lt. Kanuka!

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.540
All right, let's hurry.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:16.130
Okay.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:44.450
He's on his way!
He'll be here in ten minutes!

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:48.870
Okay, bring in machine 3,
as-is. Carrier 1: Deck-up.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:24.800
Mr. Sakaki.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.550
Is anything wrong?

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:43.570
No.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:52.740
It's nothing.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.880
Special Vehicles,
Second Section.

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:04.710
What?!

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:08.390
We have a call from District 7:
There's a 305 in Shibuya!

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:11.350
Division 2, all units:
MOVE OUT!

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:16.480
Move that carrier! Hurry up
with the revolver-cannon!

00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:19.400
So, Noa, are you getting
a feel for the place?

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:20.900
I'll say!

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:27.070
Hurry up, or I'll dump
you all in the sea!

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:17.260
In the middle of
broad daylight...

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:19.810
some tourists happened to
see a monster?

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:20.810
- A bear?
- No.

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:21.850
- A mole?
- Uhh...

00:24:21.850 --> 00:24:22.690
- A rat?
- Well...

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:23.770
- A Labor?
- I don't know!!

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:26.560
What if it's a ghost?
I'm scared!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.150
Then out of nowhere,
six shots ring out in the dark.

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:34.360
Next episode:
"Go to Demon Mountain".

00:24:34.450 --> 00:24:36.370
Target, Lock On!

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:41.580
Next episode

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:41.580
Go to Demon Mountain!
